course: dictionary
lesson: 10932
title: Vowels
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vowel is a speech sound made with your mouth open and the air flowing freely, like the sound in «cat» or «see». The letters a, e, i, o and u, and sometimes y, stand for these sounds.
explain: Consonants are the other letters, like the «t» in «cat». Sorting letters into vowels and consonants helps you read and spell. Try it: say a letter's sound and notice whether your mouth stays open and the air flows freely.
explain: Vowels can be short or long. In «hop» the o is short; in «hope» the o is long, and the e at the end is silent. Some words, like «happy», use a vowel sound at the end too.
fact: A vowel is one of the letters a, e, i, o, u, and sometimes y.
fact: «Y» is a vowel in «happy», where it says /ee/, but a consonant at the start of «yes».
fact: A syllable is a beat in a word with one vowel sound, so «sand-wich» has two syllables.
fact: Use «an» before a vowel sound, as in «an apple» or «an egg», and «a» before a consonant sound, as in «a dog».
fact: In a short word with one short vowel and one final consonant, double the consonant before -ing or -ed: «stop», «stopped».
exercise: Which letter is a vowel? | *e | t | s | b
exercise: How many vowel sounds are in «cat»? | two | *one | none | three
exercise: Which word starts with a vowel sound? | dog | yes | thin | *apple
test: In «happy», the y says /ee/. Is it a vowel or a consonant here? | *a vowel | a number | a consonant
test: Which word has a short vowel sound in the middle? | hope | *hop | hoop
exam: In «stopped», why do we double the p before -ed? | *Because it has one short vowel and one final consonant | Because it makes the word silent | Because the word is long | Because p is a vowel
